<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">North Caucasian Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Yekaterinodar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Soviet republic of 1918 uniting the Kuban, Black Sea, Terek and Stavropol soviets against the White armies.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In July 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a> merged the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kuban-black-sea-soviet-republic">Kuban-Black Sea Soviet Republic</a> with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/terek-soviet-republic">Terek Soviet Republic</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/stavropol-soviet-republic">Stavropol Soviet Republic</a>, creating the North Caucasian Soviet Republic as part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>. Its first capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a>. The merger was meant to unite Red forces in the south against the advancing White armies and hostile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was governed by a central executive committee and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Denikin</a>, which took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a> in August 1918 and forced the government to move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyatigorsk">Pyatigorsk</a>. Its large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> forces suffered from poor discipline and quarrels between party leaders and commanders, culminating in the commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-sorokin">Ivan Sorokin's</a> arrest and execution of the republic's leaders in October 1918.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-sorokin">Sorokin</a> was himself killed, and by the end of 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">Whites</a> had crushed the republic's army; it was abolished in December 1918. Its remnants retreated towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan">Astrakhan</a>, and Soviet rule returned to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> only in 1920.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/north-caucasian-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="North Caucasian Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Yekaterinodar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abram Rubin, Ivan Sorokin</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>North Caucasus SR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=north-caucasian-soviet-republic" aria-label="North Caucasian Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5712 618 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where North Caucasian Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6032 874L6032 874M6032 874L5927 843M6032 874L5999 843M6032 874L5820 533M6032 874L6611 554"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6032 874h0M5927 843h0M5999 843h0M5820 533h0M6611 554h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6032 874h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6032 874h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=north-caucasian-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
